Write an original story for upper elementary aged children (9-12 years old). The length should be approximately 400 words. The theme is a butterfly and human become friends. The style should be appropriate for the children's reading level and include figures of speech that are observed at this reading stage.
//
Make the main character complex (not one dimensional) and fully-fledged.
//
Subtly introduce a lesson about death , which is a part of life, just like grief. The butterfly dies.
//
Start the story from medias res. Focus on the final moments of the butterfly's life and show how greatly this impacts the protagonist - it needn't end on a positive note.

